id: ops-k9iv
title: "pm CLI 2026.9.11 drops every pm-ops command, because its new core ops group collides at group level"
description: "Measured 2026-09-12 while certifying pm CLI 2026.9.12. From 2026.9.11, pm-cli registers a core ops command group (stats, health, validate, gc, telemetry, eval, test-all), and extension collision is decided per group, not per leaf. All ten pm-ops commands (ops audit, docstrings, merge-receipts, metrics, outdated, policy, report, scan, status, verify-release) are dropped with extension_command_collision and core command preserved, although none of those leaves exists in core. Reproduced by installing this package into a fresh project: pm ops metrics prints usage on 2026.9.10 and fails with Unknown command metrics on 2026.9.11 and 2026.9.12. The package test 'installed pm CLI routes --repos values to every fleet command' fails on 2026.9.12 for exactly this reason. Library consumers that import pm-ops/attestation are unaffected, so the fleet's release gates keep working; the pm command surface is what breaks. Filed upstream as unbraind/pm-cli#1249."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-12T21:25:15.228Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-17T19:42:53.865Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-17T19:42:53.825Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-17T19:42:53.825Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: claude-orchestrator
acceptance_criteria: "Either pm-cli ships leaf-level collision detection, so pm ops metrics works with pm-ops installed on a CLI that has the core ops group, and this repository then certifies that CLI with its routing test passing unchanged; or pm-ops moves its commands to a namespace core does not own, with a documented migration path and the routing test updated to the new paths"
repro_steps: "1. Pin @unbrained/pm-cli to 2026.9.17 in pm-ops. 2. Run: ./node_modules/.bin/pm ops --help. 3. Verify all 10 pm-ops leaves register alongside 7 core ops. 4. Run: ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --output-budget unbounded. 5. Verify extension health ok, activation_failure_count: 0."
resolution: Upstream defect fixed in pm CLI 2026.9.14 by pm-bwkmp4 (Allow non-colliding extension leaves beneath core command groups). pm-ops pinned binary upgraded to 2026.9.17.
expected_result: "All ten pm-ops leaves register under pm ops alongside core's seven (stats, health, validate, gc, telemetry, eval, test-all), with extension health ok and activation_failure_count: 0"
actual_result: "Measured with pinned binary 2026.9.17: 10/10 pm-ops leaves registered (audit, docstrings, merge-receipts, metrics, outdated, policy, report, scan, status, verify-release) alongside 7/7 core ops (stats, health, validate, gc, telemetry, eval, test-all). Extension health ok=true, activation_failure_count=0, migration failed_count=0."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-17T19:41:27.038Z",pi-agent,"Reproduced 2026-09-17 with pm-ops pinned binary @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.17:\n\n$ ./node_modules/.bin/pm ops --help\nCommands (pm-ops extension leaves, 10/10 registered):\n  audit, docstrings, merge-receipts, metrics, outdated, policy, report, scan, status, verify-release\nCommands (core ops, 7/7 registered):\n  stats, health, validate, gc, telemetry, eval, test-all\n\n$ ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --output-budget unbounded\nextensions check: status=ok, ok=true\n  discovered: pm-ops v2026.8.31, status=ok, enabled=true\n  activation: command_handler_count=10, parser_override_count=10, commands=10\n  contributions.commands: [ops audit, ops docstrings, ops merge-receipts, ops metrics, ops outdated, ops policy, ops report, ops scan, ops status, ops verify-release]\ntriage: status=ok, load_failure_count=0, activation_failure_count=0, migration_failed_count=0\nmigration_status: failed_count=0\nhost_version: 2026.9.17\n\nAll ten pm-ops leaves register under `pm ops` alongside core's seven. Extension health ok, activation_failure_count: 0."
